{{also|pre-position|préposition}}

==English==
{{wikipedia|preposition|mul=English prepositions}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*tḱey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|preposicioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|preposicion}}, from {{der|en|la|praepositio|praepositio, praepositionem}}, from {{m|la|praepono||to place before}}, equivalent to {{pre|en|pre|position}}. Compare {{cog|fr|préposition}}. So called because it is placed before the word with which it is phrased, as in {{m|en||a bridge '''[[of]]''' iron}}, {{m|en||he comes '''[[from]]''' town}}, {{m|en||it is good '''[[for]]''' food}}, {{m|en||he escaped '''[[by]]''' running}}.

